/* ============================================================================
   دندنها — the songs (1 Oct 2026)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Egyptian songs only, family-clean: the classics (أم كلثوم، عبد الحليم، عبد
   الوهاب، فريد، شادية، وردة، نجاة…), the pop of the 90s to the 2010s (عمرو دياب،
   منير، أنغام، شيرين، تامر، حماقي…) and the mahraganat and the newest.

   Two sources of the official 30-second previews (the owner, 1 Oct 2026), both
   free with no key: Apple (https://itunes.apple.com/lookup?id=…) and Deezer
   (https://api.deezer.com/track/…). Every song is pinned to ONE of them -
   { src: 'itunes', id } or { src: 'deezer', id }, the ORIGINAL singer's
   recording with a preview (the singer's own page; covers, karaoke, belly-dance,
   remix and instrumental albums left out); Apple where it had the song, Deezer
   for what Apple was missing (الأطلال، ألف ليلة وليلة، حدوتة مصرية، البخت…) and
   much of the newest. `also` is a second pin to the same singer's recording on
   the other source, tried when the first fails. An Apple pin also keeps its
   preview's address (`u`): Apple's lookup answers 403 to Cloudflare's servers
   while its audio files load fine from there, so the rooms server plays `u`
   directly, and `npm run check:songs -- --fix` keeps the addresses current.
   Otherwise only ids are kept: Deezer's
   preview addresses are signed and expire within hours (hdnea=exp=…), so the
   rooms server looks a song up each time it plays it (rooms-worker/src/songs.js)
   and streams it for one round's opaque address (/song/CODE/TOKEN), so no id,
   source, title or singer reaches a guesser's phone.

   Fields: src and id (the pin), also (the second pin, optional), t (the Arabic
   title), alt (other names the table calls it by - the famous line - judged like
   the title), s (the singer in Arabic), era ('classic' | 'pop' | 'new': the four
   choices come from the same era when they can), en (the English title, an
   answer too), se (the singer in English). A guess is judged by guessVerdict
   against t, alt and en; the singer alone is never an answer.

   Server-only (rooms-worker/build.mjs FILES): the page never needs the list.
   `npm run check` (tools/validate-content.js) checks it offline; `npm run
   check:songs` in tools/ asks both sources about every pin (--play: the
   previews themselves).
   ========================================================================= */
